# PlaySapien — root _headers
#
# Cloudflare Pages honours exactly ONE _headers file, at the deployed root.
# Audit B2: Sojourner's build used to write its own, which under the unified
# site would land at /sojourner/_headers — inert, publicly fetchable, and with
# every pattern wrong by one path segment.
#
# This file is the merge point. Each game's build emits a fragment
# (dist/_headers.fragment) already prefixed with its own path; the deploy step
# concatenates them below the platform block. Keep the fragments and this file
# in step — the fragments are the source of truth for per-game rules.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- sojourner
# from games/sojourner/src/build.py -> dist/_headers.fragment
/sojourner/assets/detail/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/sojourner/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
/sojourner/three.min.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
/sojourner/app.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/sojourner/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- wordchain
# Word Chain inlines everything into one HTML file, so it has no asset rules —
# but audit B2 notes it never had the two lines its own images needed either.
/wordchain/og.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
/wordchain/icon-512.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

# -------------------------------------------------------------------- api
# The Worker sets its own headers; this is belt and braces for anything Pages
# would otherwise be free to cache.
/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store
